## Database: Supabase PostgreSQL

### Overview

The TourWise platform uses Supabase (PostgreSQL) with the following main tables:
- `profiles` - Core user profile data
- `travel_agent` - Agent-specific information
- `itinerary` - User travel itineraries
- `booking` - Trip bookings
- `booking_passengers` - Passenger details for bookings
- `external_bookings` - Bookings for external provider trips (Service Integration Layer)
- `external_booking_passengers` - Passenger details for external bookings
- `external_payments` - Payment records for external bookings
- `external_trip_snapshots` - Optional snapshots of external listings at ingest/search time
- `payments` - Payment records for bookings
- `booking_notifications` - Booking-related notifications
- `trips` - Trips offered by agents
- `recommendation` - User reviews/recommendations for trips
- `bus_pooling_requests` - Bus pooling requests between travel agents
- `agent_messages` - Messages between travel agents
- `favorites` - User wishlist/favorites for trips
- `notification_preferences` - User-level notification channel and category settings
- `trip_images` - Multi-image gallery for trips
- `trip_categories`, `trip_tags` - Classification metadata for trips
- `trip_category_map`, `trip_tag_map` - Trip-to-category/tag mappings
- `trip_amenities`, `trip_amenity_map` - Amenity metadata and trip mappings
- `agent_specializations`, `travel_agent_specialization_map` - Agent specialization metadata and mappings
- `booking_change_history` - Immutable booking change/audit events
- `cancellation_policies`, `trip_cancellation_policy_map` - Cancellation policy definitions and per-trip overrides
- `admin_roles`, `user_admin_roles` - Admin authorization model
- `audit_logs` - System-wide auditable event log
- `waitlist_entries` - Waitlist lifecycle for full trips
- `promotions`, `promotion_trip_map`, `promotion_category_map`, `promotion_agent_map` - Promo definitions and targeting
- `promotion_redemptions` - Applied promo records by booking/user
- `group_discount_rules` - Group-seat discount configuration
- `trip_availability_rules`, `trip_blackout_dates` - Calendar rules and date-specific overrides
- `traveler_agent_conversations`, `traveler_agent_messages` - Traveler-to-agent messaging
- `commission_rules`, `commission_trip_map`, `commission_category_map`, `commission_agent_map`, `commission_ledger` - Commission policy and accounting

### Source of Truth Policy

- `database-schema.mdc` is the canonical schema reference for this repository.
- Use this file as the primary source for table names, columns, relationships, and enum semantics.
- ERD screenshots are useful visual references, but may omit fields due to zoom/layout limits.
- If screenshot, code, and docs differ, reconcile by preserving the superset of valid information in this file.

### Backend API vs. tables (this repository)

FastAPI routers under `backend/app/api/` exercise these Supabase tables today:

| Router | Tables |
|--------|--------|
| `auth.py`, `profile.py` | `travel_agent`, `profiles` |
| `trips.py` | `trips`, `travel_agent` (join), `trip_images`; merged list includes external offers from `app.integrations` (no `trips` row) |
| `bookings.py` | `booking`, `trips`, `booking_passengers`, `payments`, `travel_agent`, `booking_notifications`, `external_bookings`, `external_booking_passengers`, `external_payments` |
| `favorites.py` | `favorites`, `trips` |
| `collaboration.py` | `travel_agent`, `trips`, `bus_pooling_requests`, `agent_messages`, `booking` |
| `notification_preferences.py` | `notification_preferences` |
| `notifications.py` | `booking_notifications` |
| `integrations.py` | (read-only adapters; no direct Supabase tables) |

SQL snippets checked into `backend/supabase/` (not an exhaustive schema dump): `schema_reference.sql` (columns/tables the FastAPI layer touches), `add_trips_image_url.sql`, `storage_trip_images_bucket.sql`, `optional_profiles_trigger.sql`, `external_integrations_phase1.sql` (external SIL tables — run in Supabase SQL Editor).

**Maintenance:** When adding or changing `supabase.table(...)` usage in `backend/app/api/`, extend `backend/supabase/schema_reference.sql` using its existing comment-block style. When the actual database gains tables, columns, or relationships, update this `database-schema.mdc` file as well.

