## Table: `itinerary`

**Purpose:** Stores travel itineraries created by users.

**Columns:**
- `itinerary_id` (int8, PRIMARY KEY) - Auto-incrementing itinerary identifier
- `user_id` (uuid, FOREIGN KEY) - References `profiles.id` or `auth.users.id`
- `name` (text) - Itinerary name/title
- `start_date` (date) - Trip start date
- `end_date` (date) - Trip end date
- `status` (itinerary_status_enum) - Status enum (e.g., 'planned', 'active', 'completed', 'cancelled')
- `created_at` (timestamptz) - Creation timestamp
- `updated_at` (timestamptz) - Last update timestamp

**Relationships:**
- `user_id` → `profiles.id` (many-to-one)
- Referenced by `itinerary_id` in: `booking`

**Key Notes:**
- Users can have multiple itineraries
- Itineraries can contain multiple bookings
- `updated_at` tracks when itinerary was last modified

