## Table: `booking_notifications`

**Purpose:** Stores booking-related notifications for users.

**Columns:**
- `notification_id` (int8, PRIMARY KEY) - Auto-incrementing notification identifier
- `booking_id` (int8, FOREIGN KEY) - References `booking.booking_id`
- `user_id` (uuid, FOREIGN KEY) - References `profiles.id` or `auth.users.id`
- `notification_type` (text) - Type of notification ('booking_confirmed', 'payment_received', 'trip_reminder', 'cancellation', 'refund_processed', etc.)
- `title` (text) - Notification title
- `message` (text) - Notification message content
- `is_read` (boolean) - Whether notification has been read by user (default: false)
- `created_at` (timestamptz) - Notification creation timestamp

**Relationships:**
- `booking_id` → `booking.booking_id` (many-to-one)
- `user_id` → `profiles.id` (many-to-one)

**Key Notes:**
- Notifications are created for various booking events
- `is_read` flag tracks read status for unread notification counts
- Notifications can be filtered by `user_id` and `is_read` for efficient querying
- Used for in-app notifications and can be extended for email/push notifications

