## Table: `external_bookings`

**Purpose:** Records bookings made **through TourWise** for trips supplied by an **external** provider. Persisted **after** adapter/provider confirmation (mock or real). Local bookings remain in `booking` + `trips`.

**Columns:**
- `external_booking_id` (int8, PRIMARY KEY, identity)
- `user_id` (uuid, FOREIGN KEY) - References `profiles.id`
- `provider_id` (text, NOT NULL)
- `external_ref` (text, NOT NULL) - Provider trip/offer id at time of booking
- `synthetic_trip_id` (int8, nullable) - Optional UI `trip_id` used in routes (e.g. synthetic external id)
- `booking_date` (timestamptz) - When the booking was recorded in TourWise
- `status` (text, NOT NULL, default `confirmed`) - Align with local booking lifecycle literals where applicable (`confirmed`, `cancelled`, etc.)
- `number_of_seats` (int4, NOT NULL, > 0)
- `total_price` (numeric, NOT NULL, >= 0)
- `passenger_names` (text[]) - Quick reference array (mirror `booking`)
- `contact_email`, `contact_phone` (text, NOT NULL)
- `special_requests` (text, nullable)
- `booking_reference` (text, NOT NULL, UNIQUE) - TourWise-facing code; prefer prefix distinct from local `TW-...` (e.g. `EXT-...`)
- `provider_confirmation_ref` (text, nullable) - Id returned by provider on success
- `confirmed_at` (timestamptz, nullable)
- `cancelled_at` (timestamptz, nullable)
- `cancellation_reason` (text, nullable)
- `refund_amount` (numeric, nullable)
- `provider_response` (jsonb, nullable) - Audit of provider confirmation payload
- `created_at`, `updated_at` (timestamptz)

**Relationships:**
- `user_id` → `profiles.id` (many-to-one)
- Referenced by `external_booking_id` in: `external_booking_passengers`, `external_payments`

**Key Notes:**
- Does **not** reference `trips.trip_id` (external inventory is not TourWise `trips` rows).
- Must **not** decrement `trips.available_seats` when creating these rows (Phase 2 API responsibility).

